<title>VENEZUELA: RESEARCH ALERT-Vencemos started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Vencemos started.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>-- Credit Lyonnias said it had started coverage of Venezuelan cement company Vencemos with a buy rating.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Rafael Diaz wrote in a research note that Vencemos was &quot;one of the most profitable companies in Latin America.&quot;</p>
<p>-- With a target share price for the end of 1997 of 2,050 bolivars or $3.83, Diaz said &quot;this represents a potential price appreciation of 63 percent in local currency or 40 percent in US dollars.  We rate the shares a buy.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Venecemos is a 63.4 percent owned subsidiary of Mexico's Cemex CA</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
